

- action(n5, "check if terms and conditions need to be sorted out") & branch(b2, XOR): Omits the documented decision "check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy" and its conditional paths ("If the candidate has not accepted, the process continues. On the other hand, if the candidate has accepted, further investigation is required."), jumping directly to the next branch. (Violates SMC1, SMC4)
- action(n10, "was the form authorized by the external approver?") & action(n12, "contact external approver for clarification"): Hallucinates process steps. The source only states "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form. However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues.", with no clarification contact or secondary authorization check. (Violates SMC1, SMC2)
- action(n11, "scan and record form in GovSource"): Skips the documented step "the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation, which is received by the client HR." before reaching HR scanning/recording. (Violates SMC1)
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): Lumps all nodes under a single generic actor, whereas the source explicitly assigns responsibilities to distinct roles: "recruitment manager", "next level manager", "client HR", "TS HR coordinator", "HR representative", and "candidate". (Violates SMC7)
- branch(b9, XOR): Missing the documented continuation path for the condition "Otherwise, if the candidate accepts, the process continues." The branch only routes to renegotiation (n30) or direct convergence (c4). (Violates SMC1, SMC4)
- action(n28, "send commencement pack and letter of appointment"): Positioned sequentially after converge(c3) (post accept/decline resolution), contradicting the source instruction "Simultaneously, the commencement pack and letter of appointment are sent to the candidate." which implies concurrency. (Violates SMC4)
- defines(v1 through v10, "...", {}): All decision variables use empty ranges {}, failing to capture the explicit value spaces and thresholds described in the source (e.g., boolean acceptance/rejection, "12% rate", "40% rate"). (Violates SMC6)